xt":"The ***dissipation influence*** will move a property towards a background value over time.  In this case we are dissipating the *volume_fog_density* value, allowing the fire to \"fade out\".\n\nThe two ***turbulence influence*** compounds"},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"random value generator"},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"To make something burn, you must induce combustion.  That is, as the temperature gets hot enough, the fuel (set above) will ignite, producing flames."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"The solver settings compound specifies all the settings to be fed into the simulation.  These settings control the behavior of the simulation."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"Where it all comes together.  The solver calculates the simulation and outputs the volumes."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"We assign an Arnold material to the output volume so that the viewport matches the final rendered image as closely as possible.  We're also assigning a surface material to the \"barrel\" cylinder for the same reason."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"The **if** statement's *condition* input gives you the ability to switch between  resolutions, enabling a faster setup (*low resolution*) and a high-res final (*high resolution*)"}],"_backdrops":[{"type":"backdrop","title":"Source"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Settings"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Influences"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Simulate"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Dummy Geo"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Double-click for more info"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Vary Source Property"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Source Fuel"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Double-click for more info"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Combustion"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Assign Materials"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Resolution Switch"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Collider"}]},"ports":[{"portName":"fire_volume","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"},{"portName":"barrel_geo","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"}],"terminal_